@@ -31,9 +31,11 @@ equal and not 0. ``repeat`` must be -1.
 The sum of the four times is the flash period. The driver rounds it up to the
 next step of 128 ms, between 256 ms (128 ms on the ET6326) and 16384 ms.
 
-The flash period, the on time and the ramp times are shared by all LEDs of a
-chip. When several LEDs blink or breathe at once, they all follow the timing
-that was set last.
+The chip has two on timers, which share the flash period and the ramp times.
+Each LED that blinks or breathes gets a timer of its own, so two LEDs can do it
+at once, as long as their periods and ramps are the same. When they are not, or
+for a third LED, ``hw_pattern`` fails with -EBUSY and blinking falls back to
+the software timer.
 
 For example, to breathe with a period of 4 seconds::
 
diff --git a/drivers/leds/rgb/leds-ktd202x.c b/drivers/leds/rgb/leds-ktd202x.c
index 56a06a9..cf46f65 100644
